From b8f22961448d6130d72cc4913ad134a8686794b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:58:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ci(zig): move the macOS leg from macos-14 to macos-15

test-zig (macos-14) was not assigned a runner in any of four attempts on
2026-11-08 and -09 (runner_id 0, cancelled before a step ran), where it
passed on main on 2026-10-19. macos-15 rather than macos-latest: under the
0.13 pin the macOS 26 SDK on macos-latest left every libc symbol undefined,
and 0.16 has not been measured against it. macos-15 is arm64, so it takes
the macosx_12_0_arm64 wheel zig-requirements.txt already hashes, and its
SDK is the nearest to the 14 this leg last linked against. The two
comments that named the macos-14 pin now say what they hold.

Checks: build.yml parses as YAML. actionlint is not installed in the
session that wrote this, so it was not run, and the leg itself is
unmeasured until a run picks it up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01U3n7wUnBkRMxEHfh2ckvQ7
---
 .github/workflows/build.yml | 16 ++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/build.yml b/.github/workflows/build.yml
index 44bef58..11d762a 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/build.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/build.yml
@@ -401,12 +401,12 @@ jobs:
     runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}
     strategy:
       matrix:
-        # macos-14 is held over from the 0.13 pin, where the macOS 26 SDK on
-        # macos-latest left every libc symbol undefined and macos-14 (arm64,
-        # SDK 14) was the last image that linked. 0.16 is expected to handle
-        # the newer SDK, but that has not been measured on a runner, so the
-        # image moves in its own change rather than inside the version bump.
-        os: [ubuntu-latest, macos-14, windows-latest]
+        # macos-15, not -latest: under the 0.13 pin the macOS 26 SDK on
+        # macos-latest left every libc symbol undefined, and 0.16 has not been
+        # measured against it yet. macos-14, the last image measured, stopped
+        # being assigned runners in November 2026. macos-15 is the same arm64
+        # wheel and the nearest SDK to it.
+        os: [ubuntu-latest, macos-15, windows-latest]
     steps:
       - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7
       # ziglang on PyPI rather than a ziglang.org tarball. It is the Zig
@@ -421,7 +421,7 @@ jobs:
         run: |
           set -euo pipefail
           py=python3; command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1 || py=python
-          # macos-14's python3 is Homebrew's, and Homebrew marks it externally
+          # On macOS, python3 is Homebrew's, and Homebrew marks it externally
           # managed: `pip install` there does not warn, it exits 1 (PEP 668,
           # "externally-managed-environment") before zig is ever fetched. A
           # venv is the documented answer and needs no extra action. Scoped to
@@ -439,7 +439,7 @@ jobs:
           chmod +x "$bin/zig"
           echo "$bin" >> "$GITHUB_PATH"
           "$bin/zig" version
-      # Held over with the macos-14 pin above: 0.13 could not link against the
+      # Held over from the macos-14 pin: 0.13 could not link against the
       # newer Xcode SDK (undefined libc symbols) and the Command Line Tools SDK
       # still works. Harmless if 0.16 no longer needs it; unmeasured either way.
       - name: Use Command Line Tools SDK (macOS)
-- 
